1
00:00:00,810 --> 00:00:01,840
Thirty-four.

2
00:00:02,320 --> 00:00:04,461
That's how many times, on the record,

3
00:00:04,520 --> 00:00:07,741
Donald Trump said the Iran war would end soon.

4
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,860
Or that it was almost over.

5
00:00:09,880 --> 00:00:11,390
Or that a deal to end it

6
00:00:11,410 --> 00:00:12,562
was days away.

7
00:00:12,930 --> 00:00:15,120
We went through eight months of speeches,

8
00:00:15,140 --> 00:00:16,843
interviews and posts.

9
00:00:16,940 --> 00:00:19,140
We counted every one we could prove,

10
00:00:19,160 --> 00:00:20,864
with the date and the source.

11
00:00:21,300 --> 00:00:23,124
Then we looked at something else.

12
00:00:23,260 --> 00:00:25,300
We checked what bitcoin and oil actually

13
00:00:25,320 --> 00:00:27,965
did, on every one of those days.

14
00:00:28,210 --> 00:00:29,925
The answer surprised us.

15
00:00:31,546 --> 00:00:34,728
Here's every kind of promise, in his own words.

16
00:00:34,906 --> 00:00:37,989
March first. "We intended four to five weeks."

17
00:00:38,126 --> 00:00:39,726
March ninth. "Soon.

18
00:00:39,746 --> 00:00:40,731
Very soon."

19
00:00:40,906 --> 00:00:43,206
March seventeenth. "We'll be leaving in pretty

20
00:00:43,226 --> 00:00:44,746
much the very near future."

21
00:00:44,926 --> 00:00:47,834
March thirty-first. "Two or three weeks."

22
00:00:47,986 --> 00:00:51,016
April sixteenth. "It should be ending pretty soon."

23
00:00:51,216 --> 00:00:53,537
June ninth. "Two or three days."

24
00:00:53,836 --> 00:00:56,819
June eleventh. "Over the next few days."

25
00:00:57,036 --> 00:01:00,116
September ninth. "This war will end immediately

26
00:01:00,136 --> 00:01:01,501
after our election."

27
00:01:01,636 --> 00:01:04,156
October ninth. "One way or another, it's

28
00:01:04,176 --> 00:01:05,543
gonna be over soon."

29
00:01:05,696 --> 00:01:08,685
October thirtieth. "It's going to get wrapped up soon."

30
00:01:08,836 --> 00:01:11,606
November first. "We'll put it away very soon."

31
00:01:11,706 --> 00:01:13,467
And that same night: "It's going to

32
00:01:13,487 --> 00:01:15,328
be over very soon.

33
00:01:15,466 --> 00:01:16,469
Very soon."

34
00:01:16,806 --> 00:01:20,010
Thirty-four times. Here's what happened in between.

35
00:01:21,490 --> 00:01:23,971
Chapter one. Four to five weeks.

36
00:01:24,390 --> 00:01:26,490
February twenty-eighth, twenty twenty-six.

37
00:01:26,510 --> 00:01:29,272
American and Israeli strikes hit Iran.

38
00:01:29,570 --> 00:01:31,570
Iran answers by closing the Strait of

39
00:01:31,590 --> 00:01:34,110
Hormuz, the narrow channel that about a

40
00:01:34,130 --> 00:01:36,454
fifth of the world's oil passes through.

41
00:01:36,630 --> 00:01:38,650
The day before the war, US oil

42
00:01:38,670 --> 00:01:41,295
closed at sixty-seven dollars a barrel.

43
00:01:41,450 --> 00:01:45,100
Bitcoin closed near sixty-five thousand nine hundred.

44
00:01:45,330 --> 00:01:47,110
The next day, Trump gives his first

45
00:01:47,130 --> 00:01:50,217
timeline. "We intended four to five weeks."

46
00:01:50,550 --> 00:01:52,020
Oil doesn't wait.

47
00:01:52,040 --> 00:01:54,538
By March sixth, it's at ninety-one dollars.

48
00:01:54,680 --> 00:01:56,800
March ninth. Trump says the end is

49
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:59,139
coming. "Soon, very soon."

50
00:01:59,430 --> 00:02:02,400
That day, bitcoin jumps almost four percent.

51
00:02:02,540 --> 00:02:04,860
The next day, oil drops from ninety-five

52
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,381
dollars to eighty-four.

53
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:08,682
For a moment, the words work.

54
00:02:09,060 --> 00:02:10,802
But the war keeps going.

55
00:02:11,030 --> 00:02:13,823
March thirteenth. "I don't think it's gonna be long."

56
00:02:14,040 --> 00:02:16,840
March twenty-sixth. "Four to six weeks.

57
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:18,664
We're way ahead of schedule."

58
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,565
March thirty-first. "Two or three weeks."

59
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:24,726
By then, oil is above one hundred dollars.

60
00:02:25,020 --> 00:02:26,680
April first, in an address to the

61
00:02:26,700 --> 00:02:29,220
nation, he promises to finish the job

62
00:02:29,240 --> 00:02:31,348
"shortly, very shortly."

63
00:02:31,620 --> 00:02:34,160
April seventh. Oil hits its highest price

64
00:02:34,180 --> 00:02:35,400
of the whole war.

65
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:36,949
One hundred fourteen dollars.

66
00:02:37,140 --> 00:02:39,770
That night comes a two-week ceasefire.

67
00:02:39,850 --> 00:02:42,190
Bitcoin jumps two point six percent in

68
00:02:42,210 --> 00:02:45,151
one hour, to seventy-two thousand three hundred.

69
00:02:45,240 --> 00:02:47,992
The next day, oil falls sixteen percent.

70
00:02:48,190 --> 00:02:51,012
Trump calls it "Total and complete victory.

71
00:02:51,050 --> 00:02:52,313
One hundred percent."

72
00:02:52,450 --> 00:02:53,790
Five weeks had passed.

73
00:02:53,810 --> 00:02:55,214
The war had not ended.

74
00:02:56,764 --> 00:02:58,554
Chapter two. Days away.

75
00:02:58,814 --> 00:03:00,634
The ceasefire mostly held.

76
00:03:00,804 --> 00:03:02,914
But talks in Islamabad failed, and on

77
00:03:02,934 --> 00:03:05,774
April thirteenth, a US naval blockade of

78
00:03:05,794 --> 00:03:07,655
Iran's ports took effect.

79
00:03:07,834 --> 00:03:11,094
On April twenty-first, the ceasefire was extended,

80
00:03:11,114 --> 00:03:12,495
with no end date.

81
00:03:12,654 --> 00:03:14,794
In May, the US struck Iran twice

82
00:03:14,814 --> 00:03:17,216
more, and called it self-defense.

83
00:03:17,434 --> 00:03:19,956
And the deal was always almost done.

84
00:03:20,194 --> 00:03:23,056
May twenty-third. Details "will be announced shortly."

85
00:03:23,304 --> 00:03:26,417
June first. An agreement, "over the next week."

86
00:03:26,674 --> 00:03:28,837
June ninth. Signing "could be in two

87
00:03:28,857 --> 00:03:29,977
or three days."

88
00:03:30,324 --> 00:03:31,934
Bitcoin didn't wait for it.

89
00:03:31,954 --> 00:03:34,414
From May thirty-first to June second, it

90
00:03:34,434 --> 00:03:36,434
fell more than nine percent.

91
00:03:36,704 --> 00:03:38,414
By June thirtieth, it was at fifty-eight

92
00:03:38,434 --> 00:03:39,798
thousand five hundred.

93
00:03:40,004 --> 00:03:43,098
June seventeenth. Finally, a signed paper.

94
00:03:43,224 --> 00:03:46,498
The Islamabad Memorandum, with sixty days to negotiate.

95
00:03:46,654 --> 00:03:48,414
The next day, the US ended the

96
00:03:48,434 --> 00:03:50,759
blockade, and Hormuz reopened.

97
00:03:50,884 --> 00:03:54,299
By early July, oil had slid below seventy dollars.

98
00:03:54,574 --> 00:03:56,719
For three weeks, it looked over.

99
00:03:58,399 --> 00:04:00,600
Chapter three. "I think it's over."

100
00:04:00,969 --> 00:04:04,400
July eighth. Iran attacks three ships in Hormuz.

101
00:04:04,649 --> 00:04:07,141
The US strikes more than eighty targets.

102
00:04:07,339 --> 00:04:10,199
Iran's Revolutionary Guards say they hit eighty-five

103
00:04:10,219 --> 00:04:12,969
US military sites in Bahrain and Kuwait.

104
00:04:13,279 --> 00:04:15,023
Trump, at the NATO summit.

105
00:04:15,043 --> 00:04:15,943
"I think it's over.

106
00:04:15,963 --> 00:04:17,884
I don't want to deal with them any more."

107
00:04:18,219 --> 00:04:21,369
This time, "over" meant the ceasefire.

108
00:04:21,549 --> 00:04:23,419
Bitcoin fell about two and a half

109
00:04:23,439 --> 00:04:25,946
percent, to around sixty-two thousand.

110
00:04:26,219 --> 00:04:28,629
July thirteenth. Trump says the blockade is

111
00:04:28,649 --> 00:04:30,847
coming back, with a toll on ships.

112
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:35,999
In two trading days, Brent crude jumps eleven percent.

113
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:38,549
August sixth, in the Oval Office.

114
00:04:38,569 --> 00:04:40,289
"I don't think they can go much longer."

115
00:04:40,549 --> 00:04:43,610
By late August, the war is six months old.

116
00:04:43,710 --> 00:04:45,419
It has cost the US more than

117
00:04:45,439 --> 00:04:47,951
thirty-seven and a half billion dollars.

118
00:04:48,199 --> 00:04:50,289
Before the war, about one hundred thirty

119
00:04:50,309 --> 00:04:52,129
ships a day crossed Hormuz.

120
00:04:52,149 --> 00:04:54,453
On August twenty-sixth, twenty-four did.

121
00:04:54,829 --> 00:04:56,333
Then the tone changes.

122
00:04:56,409 --> 00:04:58,049
He's "not in a hurry" to get

123
00:04:58,069 --> 00:04:59,574
Iran back to the table.

124
00:04:59,669 --> 00:05:01,829
He posts. "Mission accomplished.

125
00:05:01,849 --> 00:05:03,069
Twenty twenty-six."

126
00:05:04,806 --> 00:05:06,956
Chapter four. After the election.

127
00:05:07,256 --> 00:05:09,776
September ninth, at Joint Base Andrews.

128
00:05:09,796 --> 00:05:12,797
"This war will end immediately after our election."

129
00:05:13,116 --> 00:05:16,358
That week, US oil crossed one hundred dollars again.

130
00:05:16,576 --> 00:05:18,578
Three days later, in Ireland.

131
00:05:18,598 --> 00:05:21,138
"I think it'll be right after the midterms, actually."

132
00:05:21,416 --> 00:05:24,519
"And oil will come tumbling down when that happens."

133
00:05:24,776 --> 00:05:27,156
October second, at a rally in Mobile,

134
00:05:27,176 --> 00:05:29,716
Alabama. "It's going to end very soon,

135
00:05:29,736 --> 00:05:31,900
and probably right after the midterms."

136
00:05:32,116 --> 00:05:34,320
October eighth, on Truth Social.

137
00:05:34,396 --> 00:05:35,920
The blockade stays.

138
00:05:36,106 --> 00:05:37,856
But "we will not be attacking Iran

139
00:05:37,876 --> 00:05:40,581
at any time prior to the Midterm Elections."

140
00:05:40,896 --> 00:05:43,756
October ninth. "One way or another, it's

141
00:05:43,776 --> 00:05:45,001
gonna be over soon."

142
00:05:45,356 --> 00:05:48,642
October thirtieth. "It's going to get wrapped up soon."

143
00:05:48,936 --> 00:05:51,706
November first. Before a rally in Iowa.

144
00:05:51,726 --> 00:05:53,456
"We'll put it away very soon, one

145
00:05:53,476 --> 00:05:54,643
way or the other."

146
00:05:54,856 --> 00:05:55,836
On stage that night.

147
00:05:55,856 --> 00:05:58,476
"It's going to be over very soon.

148
00:05:58,496 --> 00:05:59,486
Very soon."

149
00:05:59,736 --> 00:06:02,056
And. "At some point, we're going to

150
00:06:02,076 --> 00:06:03,544
have to give them the hammer."

151
00:06:03,826 --> 00:06:05,886
By the end of October, the Pentagon

152
00:06:05,906 --> 00:06:09,665
counted twenty-three American service members killed in the war.

153
00:06:09,956 --> 00:06:12,565
Oil was up about seventy percent from

154
00:06:12,585 --> 00:06:13,705
a year earlier.

155
00:06:15,275 --> 00:06:17,905
Chapter five. Did the market believe him?

156
00:06:18,325 --> 00:06:20,486
Here's the part we didn't expect.

157
00:06:20,645 --> 00:06:23,075
We lined up all thirty-four statements against

158
00:06:23,095 --> 00:06:24,346
the daily prices.

159
00:06:24,626 --> 00:06:27,226
He said it on thirty-one different days.

160
00:06:27,445 --> 00:06:29,685
Bitcoin closed higher on sixteen of them,

161
00:06:29,705 --> 00:06:31,467
and lower on fifteen.

162
00:06:31,565 --> 00:06:32,825
That's a coin flip.

163
00:06:33,225 --> 00:06:36,025
Oil? In the trading session on or

164
00:06:36,045 --> 00:06:38,805
after his statements, US oil went up

165
00:06:38,825 --> 00:06:41,188
nineteen times out of twenty-seven.

166
00:06:41,235 --> 00:06:43,368
The words said "almost over."

167
00:06:43,425 --> 00:06:45,788
The oil price kept saying "not yet."

168
00:06:46,085 --> 00:06:48,515
The biggest moves didn't come from words.

169
00:06:48,535 --> 00:06:49,809
They came from events.

170
00:06:49,975 --> 00:06:51,605
The April seventh ceasefire.

171
00:06:51,625 --> 00:06:52,655
The June memorandum.

172
00:06:52,675 --> 00:06:54,015
The July eighth collapse.

173
00:06:54,035 --> 00:06:55,049
The blockade.

174
00:06:55,195 --> 00:06:56,955
From the day before the first strike

175
00:06:56,975 --> 00:07:00,925
to November second, bitcoin rose about sixteen percent.

176
00:07:01,035 --> 00:07:03,025
By late October, US oil was up

177
00:07:03,045 --> 00:07:04,775
about fifty-four percent.

178
00:07:06,370 --> 00:07:08,210
His side, and the count.

179
00:07:08,630 --> 00:07:10,132
Trump has his own answer.

180
00:07:10,290 --> 00:07:12,353
On October first, he said his "four

181
00:07:12,373 --> 00:07:14,450
to six weeks" meant the Iran nuclear

182
00:07:14,470 --> 00:07:17,615
threat, which he says he ended "in one night."

183
00:07:17,950 --> 00:07:20,016
Other counts use other rules.

184
00:07:20,170 --> 00:07:22,857
Axios counted twelve signals by March thirtieth.

185
00:07:23,018 --> 00:07:25,530
CNN counted thirty-eight times he said a

186
00:07:25,550 --> 00:07:27,970
deal was close, by June ninth.

187
00:07:28,110 --> 00:07:30,730
Our rule. One dated, public statement per

188
00:07:30,750 --> 00:07:32,181
place, per day.

189
00:07:32,240 --> 00:07:35,063
All thirty-four sources are in the description.

190
00:07:36,683 --> 00:07:38,524
So what's the lesson for traders?

191
00:07:38,883 --> 00:07:41,025
One. A promise isn't a price.

192
00:07:41,153 --> 00:07:44,366
Bitcoin treated thirty-four "soons" like noise.

193
00:07:44,623 --> 00:07:46,987
Two. Watch what you can measure.

194
00:07:47,123 --> 00:07:49,368
Ships through the Strait of Hormuz.

195
00:07:49,423 --> 00:07:51,529
The blockade. A signed paper.

196
00:07:51,563 --> 00:07:53,403
Those moved the market.

197
00:07:53,733 --> 00:07:56,863
Three. When someone says "soon," ask: soon

198
00:07:56,883 --> 00:07:58,083
compared to what?

199
00:07:58,343 --> 00:08:00,003
Four to five weeks has now lasted

200
00:08:00,023 --> 00:08:01,352
more than eight months.

201
00:08:01,763 --> 00:08:03,993
The midterms were on November third.

202
00:08:04,013 --> 00:08:06,775
He said the war would end right after.

203
00:08:07,133 --> 00:08:08,815
Will it end soon this time?

204
00:08:09,213 --> 00:08:10,816
Tell us in the comments.

205
00:08:11,203 --> 00:08:12,653
Follow Chain Secrets.

206
00:08:12,673 --> 00:08:14,597
Every chart hides a story.
